      "body": "## Background\n\nFixes #44189\n\n## Problem\n\nThe `/start_profile` endpoint accepts caller-controlled `profile_prefix` and `profile_id`. These were used directly to construct trace filenames without sanitizing path separators. A relative `profile_prefix` containing `..` or an absolute `profile_prefix` could let the caller escape the requested `output_dir`.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdded `_sanitize_filename_component()` helper that:\n- Uses `os.path.basename()` to strip any directory component\n- Replaces path separators and `..` sequences with underscores\n- Filters out other potentially dangerous characters\n\nApplied sanitization to both `profile_prefix` and `profile_id` in:\n- `profiler_manager.py` (V1 profiler / `SchedulerProfilerManager._init_profile`)\n- `profile_utils.py` (V2 profiler / `ProfileManager.configure`)\n\n## Test\n\n```python\nsanitize(\"../escaped\")           # -> \"escaped\"\nsanitize(\"/etc/passwd/escaped\")  # -> \"escaped\"  \nsanitize(\"../../etc/malicious\")   # -> \"malicious\"\nsanitize(\"my-profile-id\")         # -> \"my-profile-id\"  (normal case preserved)\n```\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38556055730](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38556055730)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38556055697](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38556055697)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38556055733](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38556055733)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
